<title>UK: Grand Met bucks weak market on revamp hopes.</title>
<headline>Grand Met bucks weak market on revamp hopes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in food and drink company Grand Metropolitan Plc bucked a generally weaker stock market on Friday, rising over 1.5 percent on a positive report in the Financial Times about the company's restructuring. .</p>
<p>Grand Met shares were up 7-1/2p at 479p at 0756 GMT while the overall market was weaker, hit by worries about U.S. jobs data scheduled for release at 1230 GMT.</p>
<p>The FT's influential Lex column praised Grand Met's restructuring plans and said a share buyback could be possible.</p>
<p>&quot;Trade is pretty thin but this report helped stir some interest early on,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
